{{Quote|Gus looks so much like a ghost child that he's often mistaken for one. Perhaps fittingly, he's an enthusiast of all things Supernatural, since he's too innocent to be scared.}}
{{Portrait}}
Gus is a {{Rarity|Super Rare}} [[Brawler]] who has moderate health and damage, but with a very long range, immense utility with his Super, and unique healing capabilities. He was the 60th Brawler added to the game. He attacks by throwing a long-ranged balloon at enemies, dealing moderate damage. Gus charges up a bar by hitting enemy Brawlers, and charging it makes his next attack spawn a spirit that heals him or allies that pick it up. His Super grants him or a teammate a shield that absorbs damage and decays over time, pushing all nearby enemies back. His first Gadget, Kooky Popper, instantly explodes all active spirits. His second Gadget, Knockback Spirit, fires a spirit that damages and knocks enemies back. Gus' first Star Power, Health Bonanza, significantly increases the healing from his spirits. His second Star Power, Spirit Animal, momentarily increases the damage of whoever receives Gus' Super. His Hypercharge, Spooky Pop, shoots spirits that damage enemies and heal allies in all directions when Gus uses his Super on himself, and curves the spirits in a circular motion when he uses his Super on teammates.

==Attack: Loony Balloons==
{{Quote|Gus shoots balloons at enemies. After several hits, a spirit will drop. Collected spirits will restore some health to Gus or his teammates.}}Gus fires a long-ranged balloon in a straight line. Each attack that hits an enemy Brawler fills a bar by one third. After the bar is filled, the next attack that hits an enemy Brawler or mobile spawnable empties the bar and spawns a spirit at the enemy location. Spirits can be collected by Gus or his allies, healing them, but the healing doesn't scale with [[Showdown|Power Cubes]] or outside buffs. Up to 3 spirits will remain in place indefinitely until collected. Spawning more spirits causes the others to disappear in the same order they appeared. Gus' attack has a moderate cooldown of 0.5 seconds. 

==Super: Spooky Boy==
{{Quote|Gus uses Spooky (a balloon creation and also his best friend), to create a shield around himself or one of his teammates and pushes nearby enemies back.}}[[File:Hardcore Icon.png|left|40x40px|link=]]Gus launches a long-ranged balloon dog that can pass through walls and grants himself or allies a consumable shield that blocks a large amount of damage and knocks nearby enemies back. The shield decays for 5% health every 0.5 seconds, similar to [[Edgar]]'s Hardcore Gadget. The player can give teammates the shield by aiming the Super or give it to Gus himself by auto-aiming it. If an attack deals more damage than the shield's current health, the shield disappears and the Brawler with the shield is damaged by the remaining damage. [[Colette]]'s attack and Super will deal damage based on the Brawler's max health when this shield is active. Enemies damaging those with the shield on can still charge their Supers, but allies with Traits allowing them to charge Super from taking damage cannot.

==Gadgets==
===Kooky Popper===
{{Quote|Explode all uncollected spirits, dealing 2160 damage to nearby enemies. Cooldown: 16 seconds.}}{{Gadget|1}}
When activated, all spirits within 14 tiles of Gus' location explode, dealing the same amount of damage as Gus' main attack to enemies within 2 tiles. The amount of damage dealt can stack with other spirits. This Gadget can only be activated if there is at least 1 spirit on the battlefield close enough. This Gadget's cooldown starts 2.5 seconds after the button is pressed.

{{Quote|Nearby enemies lose 1 ammo.}}{{Buffie|Gadget}}
With the Buffie, enemies damaged by the explosion lose 1 ammo.

===Knockback Spirit===
{{Quote|Gus throws a spirit, knocking back enemies and dealing 520 damage. Cooldown: 26 seconds.}}{{Gadget|2}}
Gus throws a piercing projectile which spawns a spirit at the end of its range, knocks enemies back and deals 24.07% of his main attack damage. This Gadget does not consume ammo.

{{Quote|Create a spirit for each enemy hit.}}{{Buffie|Gadget}}
With the Buffie, the Gadget spawns a spirit whenever it hits an enemy.

==Star Powers==
===Health Bonanza===
{{Quote|Healing gained from spirits is increased by 50%.}}{{StarPower|1}}
This Star Power increases the healing by 50% from picking up a spirit.

{{Quote|Spirits move toward the nearest ally.}}{{Buffie|Star}}
With the Buffie, the spirits slowly move toward the nearest ally, including through walls. The spirits remain stationary if there are no allies to follow.

===Spirit Animal===
{{Quote|Spooky increases the damage of a teammate by 25% for 5 seconds.}}{{StarPower|2}}
Gus or allies affected by his Super will also deal 25% more damage for 5 seconds after gaining the shield. The damage boost lasts for 5 seconds even if the shield wears off sooner.

{{Quote|Spooky also gives a teammate a 15% speed boost for 5 sec.}}{{Buffie|Star}}
With the Buffie, the Super also grants Gus or allies a 15% movement speed boost for 5 seconds.

==Hypercharge: Spooky Pop==
{{Quote|On impact, Gus' Super will drop spirits in all directions that deal damage to enemies and heal teammates!}}{{Hypercharge}}
When activated, Gus' Super shoots a wave of 10 spirits for 10 tiles in all directions that damage enemies and heal allies. The spirits have a 3.33-tile wide blind spot at the center, so they cannot all hit an enemy at point-blank range. If Gus uses his Super on himself, they travel straight out, but if he uses his Super on teammates, the spirits move in a curving clockwise motion instead, similar to [[Spike]]'s Curveball Star Power. This allows them to cover a larger area and ultimately hit more targets, and it also effectively increases the range of the spirits. Gus also gains a 20% speed boost, as well as a 5% damage and shield boost. 

{{Quote|Gus' main attack becomes larger and can go through walls!}}{{Buffie|Hyper}}
With the Buffie, Gus's main attacks become larger, and can pass through obstacles. Increased Hypercharge duration by 2 seconds.

==Wasabi Power==
{{RemovedContent|section}}
{{Quote|Main attacks drop spirits with every hit!}}<div style="float: right;">[[File:Hot Wasabi.png|64px|link=]]</div>Gus' next attack spawned a spirit on every target hit.

==Tips==
===Game Modes and Maps===
*Gus' Super can be used to protect the teammate who has the most Gems or is worth the most [[Bounty]] Stars so they do not die and lose their Gems/ give the opponents Stars. It can also be used to protect whoever is holding the Ball in [[Brawl Ball]].
**In addition, if Gus or his teammate is the Gem carrier or is worth many [[Bounty]] Stars, and they're pursued by aggressive Brawlers like El Primo, [[Bull]], [[Fang]], [[Buzz]], [[Shelly]], [[Darryl]], or [[Mortis]], Gus can use his Super to knock them back and run away or stay out of their range to continue attacking.
*Gus is better used defensively and for supporting teammates. Because of this, he is more useful in 3v3 modes or [[Duo Showdown]], where he can take more advantages of his abilities.
*Gus shouldn't be underestimated when going offensive, either. With his Spirit Animal Star Power, Super, and Kooky Popper Gadget, he can deal high total damage combo, and his own survivability is ensured with his Super.

===Recommended Build===
*Gus' spirits can be very useful for area control if he's using his Kooky Popper Gadget, since he can hit enemies when they're close to the Gem Spawn in [[Gem Grab]] and put spirits in said area. Then, when enemies get close to the spawn to grab Gems, he can use the Gadget to pop the spirits and deal damage to the enemies.
*However, Knockback Spirit is generally the better Gadget, as it not only allows for very quick, immense healing, especially when paired with his Health Bonanza Starpower, but it can also be used as an anti-aggro tool whenever your Super is unavailable.
*Both Health Bonanza and Spirit Animal are suitable for Gus. When playing offensive, use his Spirit Animal Star Power to gain a damage boost when in a tight situation. This can allow Gus to finish off the enemies. If playing supportively, use the Health Bonanza Star Power as it will heal teammates a lot more. This is especially useful if your teammates are melee Brawlers e.g. Edgar, [[Rosa]], [[Kit]], [[Bibi]], Fang, Buzz, [[Sam]], [[Lily]], or [[El Primo]], as they will be close to the spirits that spawn and can heal themselves by collecting the spirits.

===Strategies===
*If playing Showdown modes with Gus e.g. [[Showdown|Solo Showdown]], he can use his Super to knock enemies into the poison gas for extra damage. This may even allow Gus to make use of the spirits he may have placed down earlier to deal more damage if using his Kooky Popper Gadget.
*Gus' Super is used best on assassins with lower health and can quickly approach enemies such as [[Leon]], [[Crow]], Mortis, [[Mico]], [[Stu]], [[Cordelius]], [[Shade]], and [[Edgar]], as they can get close to the enemies with less risk of dying quickly, and are able to wipe out the entire team.
**This could be a very effective strategy in game modes such as Brawl Ball, and gives your team enough time to easily score the ball.
**In game modes like Gem Grab or Bounty, this can be used to turn the tables on the enemy as Gus' team will get a lot of Gems/Stars.

===Other===
*Gus' Super has to be used immediately, either offensively or defensively, after activating it, since its health decays very rapidly. After a couple seconds, it won't be useful anymore.
*If giving Gus' Super shield to a teammate, aim carefully as it may miss them due to mistimed movements on both Gus' and his teammates sides. Alternatively, go closer to them so you have less chance of missing.
*It is better to pair Gus with melee [[:Category:Brawlers|Brawlers]], since his spirits are usually positioned in the enemies' side, where the close-ranged teammates could get close and receive the heal from the spirits.
*He is surprisingly able to do lots of damage at close-range and survive because he can use his shield for instant health, not to mention his ghosts that give him health. By rushing on enemies who cannot burst, he is more likely to win.

